.TH TS_TEST_MT 1 "" "" tslib
.SH NAME
ts_test_mt \- A basic multitouch test program for tslib.
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBts_test_mt\fR [OPTION]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ts_test_mt
is used to test
.B tslib
using
.BR ts_read_mt (),
see
.BR ts_read_mt (3).
It can be used for single and multi touch devices and lets you test the
input behaviour with tslib's filters applied.
Two modes are offered by buttons on the display:
.sp
In
.B Drag
mode, one crosshair for each concurrently made touch contact is drawn to
the framebuffer display.
.sp
In
.B Draw
mode, lines are drawed for each touch contact.
.sp
\fB\-r, \-\-rotate [value]\fR
.RS 4
Rotate the screen. value is 0 for 0 degree, 1 for 90 degrees (CW), 2 for
180 degrees (upside down) and 3 for 270 degrees (CCW).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Print the input samples' values to the console.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-j, \-\-slots\fR
.RS 4
Override the number of concurrent touch contacts to allocate.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-i, \-\-idev\fR
.RS 4
Explicitly choose the original input event device for tslib to use.
Default: the environment variable \fBTSLIB_TSDEVICE\fR's value.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-n, \-\-samples\fR
.RS 4
Automatically exit after having read n samples.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-a, \-\-altcross\fR
.RS 4
Show an alternative crosshair symbol at the touch points.
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ts.conf (5),
.BR ts_calibrate (1),
.BR ts_uinput (1),
.BR ts_test (1)
